# routine — a one-off act teaches nothing, and does not stop the visit teaching
#
# Catching a butterfly is not something to come back for: no routine kind is about it. It used to be
# worse than nothing — in the old chain recorder it could end the recording, so the walk after it was
# lost. Routines are entry points now and nothing ends a session's learning; this script keeps the
# guarantee that matters: catch first, walk second, leave, and the visit has taught exactly the Go to
# routine for where it left from.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --observe-only "Butterfly"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
strategy succeed

# The one-off act.
goal catch
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb catch
expect Caught:

# The walk after it, on a visit of its own. The catch changed neither the area nor the hour, so its
# CONTINUE carries the phase on rather than opening the next one; leaving and coming back opens a
# phase pinned to the field. Leaving from the area the visit opened in records nothing.
observe "Test Field"
goal move
click button
wait 60
click button
wait mode WorldView 90
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 90
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb move
expect Moved to:

observe none
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

# Only the walk: the catch taught nothing.
inspect routines
expect-state routines category=goto location=
expect-state routines Test Field
expect-no-state routines category=gather
quit
